    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-041: Pseudo-elements (`::before` / `::after`)** — the CSS feature that draws the Wikipedia title underline, `[edit]` brackets, and citation backlinks. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~400-500 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Directly closes ADR-040's deferred h1 prediction.** ADR-040 shipped border shorthand expansion expecting `h1#firstHeading` to gain a bottom underline. It didn't. Diagnostic revealed:\n- `border-bottom-width: 1px` IS on h1 (ADR-040 works)\n- But `.vector-page-titlebar .firstHeading { border: 0 }` (specificity 0,2,0) wins over `h1 { border-bottom: ... }` (0,0,1)\n- **The actual visible underline is `.vector-page-titlebar::after`** — a pseudo-element\n\nPseudo-elements are entirely missing from our engine. This ADR adds them.\n\n## Measurement\n\n| Category | Count | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `::after { content: '' }` (empty, decorative) | ~25 | Title underline, dropdown chevron |\n| `::before { content: 'literal' }` | ~12 | `[edit]` brackets, `↑` backlinks |\n| `::after { content: 'literal' }` | ~8 | Closing brackets, ` \\| ` separators |\n| `::before { content: attr(...) }` | 4 | Line numbers (deferred) |\n| `::before { content: url(...) }` | 6 | External link icons (deferred) |\n\n**~45 pseudo rules total, ~37 in scope** for this ADR.\n\n## First-viewport impact\n\n| Element | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Title \"HTML\" | No underline | **Underlined** (ADR-040 prediction achieved) |\n| Section headings | No edit link | **`[edit]` bracket text** |\n| Citations | No backlink | **`↑` backlink arrow** |\n\n**4 genuinely visible first-viewport changes.**\n\n## Three-commit cycle\n\n**Commit 1 (structural, behavior-neutral):**\n- `PseudoElement` enum + `CompoundSelector::pseudo` field\n- Parser recognizes `::before` / `::after` (both colon forms)\n- `Selector::matches(node, PseudoElement)` two-arg overload\n- `CascadeResult` struct with `element_styles` + `pseudo_styles`\n- Mechanical update to existing callers\n- **No visual change** (no pseudo rules matched today, so pseudo map is empty)\n\n**Commit 2 (visible, PNG-verified before merge):**\n- Pseudo-box synthesis in `layout_element`'s child loop\n- `content: ''` and `content: 'text'` handling\n- `position: absolute` via ADR-033\n- Title underline, edit brackets, citation backlinks appear\n- **Render-and-inspect PNG before merge** (ADR-039 lesson codified in ADR-040's Verification; carried forward here)\n\n**Commit 3 (docs):**\n- ADR-041 status → Implemented\n- **ADR-040 Post-ADR-041 correction** (h1 prediction corrected with mechanism)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Deferred (enumerated in ADR)\n\n- `content: attr() / counter() / url()` — 8 rules, small chrome\n- `::first-line` / `::first-letter` / `::selection` / `::marker` / `::placeholder` — different mechanism (sub-ranges of element's own content)\n- State-aware pseudo-elements (`:hover::after` etc.) — requires layout recalc on state change; ADR-018 state is paint-only\n- `content: '' ''` multi-quote — 0 uses\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Two-commit structural/visible split** — Commit 1 is behavior-neutral (parse + cascade only). Commit 2 is the visible change (layout + paint). Comfortable with this isolation?\n- [ ] **`content: ''` produces a box** — the title underline is `content: ''` but with `display: block; position: absolute; height: 1px; background: #a2a9b1`. Empty string literal but visible box. Real-browser behavior. Agree?\n- [ ] **`CascadeResult` return type** — cascade returns `{element_styles, pseudo_styles}` instead of `std::map`. Mechanical change at callers. Agree?\n- [ ] **State-aware pseudo-elements deferred** — `:hover::after` requires layout recalc on hover. Our ADR-018 state is paint-only. Deferring to a future ADR is honest scope. Agree?\n- [ ] **PNG verification required before merge** — Commit 2 must show title underline + edit brackets before merge. ADR-039 lesson.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. After merge, verify `main` still clean (504 cases / 1927 assertions).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/041-pseudo-elements.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #206",
